# 3-Tier Web Application on AWS

A classic 3-tier architecture (web, application, database) deployed on AWS with high availability across two Availability Zones — using an Application Load Balancer, Auto Scaling Group, and isolated subnet tiers.

## Architecture

Internet
   → Application Load Balancer (public subnets, 2 AZs)
   → Auto Scaling Group of EC2 instances (web tier, public subnets)
   → App tier (private subnets, 2 AZs)
   → RDS database (private subnets, 2 AZs, Multi-AZ)

## Design


- **Networking** : Custom VPC (10.0.0.0/16) with 6 subnets across 2 AZs — 2 public (web tier), 2 private (app tier), 2 private (DB tier)
- **Web tier**: Auto Scaling Group (min 2, max 4) behind an internet-facing Application Load Balancer, health-checked on /
- **Security**: Security groups scoped tightly — web tier only accepts traffic from the ALB, not directly from the internet
- **Availability**: Every tier spans 2 Availability Zones for fault tolerance


## Tools & services

VPC · EC2 · Application Load Balancer · Auto Scaling Group · Launch Templates · IAM · CloudFormation · Route 53

## Repo contents

├── cloudformation/
│   ├── 01-networking.yaml   # VPC, subnets, route tables
│   └── 02-web-tier.yaml     # ALB, ASG, Launch Template
├── scripts/
│   └── web-tier-userdata.sh
└── README.md

## Deploying

bash

# 1. Deploy networking layer
aws cloudformation create-stack \
  --stack-name 3tier-networking \
  --template-body file://cloudformation/01-networking.yaml

# 2. Deploy web tier (pass outputs from step 1 as parameters)
aws cloudformation create-stack \
  --stack-name 3tier-web \
  --template-body file://cloudformation/02-web-tier.yaml \
  --parameters ParameterKey=VpcId,ParameterValue=<vpc-id> \
               ParameterKey=PublicSubnetIds,ParameterValue=<subnet-a>\\,<subnet-b> \
               ParameterKey=AmiId,ParameterValue=<ami-id>

What I contributed

Contributed to the VPC/subnet design, Auto Scaling Group configuration, and CloudWatch-based health monitoring for the web tier as part of a team project at Xortican Technologies.

Notes

Rebuilt and documented as a portfolio piece based on hands-on architecture work. The app and database tiers (private subnets) are provisioned but application/DB layer templates are a work in progress — networking and web tier are complete and deployable as-is.
